Extremely clever, I'd say.  There are many problems that are unwieldly for
serial processing that could be attacked with such a recipe.  The key as
always is to find a good way to represent the problem that facilitates the
selection mechanism.  (What are the "well-established techniques of molecular
biology" that can select out desirable strands, anyway?)

I only read the above, but it seems that the problem being solved isn't quite
the travelling salesman problem.  It seems that the _distance_ between cities
is not being represented, only the presence of a path.  (I may have
misunderstood).  So it seems like the question being answered is whether there
is a route, not which is the shortest.  Anyway, it seems possible to represent
the distance by inserting appropriate lengths of arbitrary non-city sequences
into the `flight numbers' and then selecting by length...  Anyone know more
details?

